<title>USA: Philips, Osram Sylvania settle ad dispute.</title>
<headline>Philips, Osram Sylvania settle ad dispute.</headline>
<dateline>SOMERSET, N.J. 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philips Lighting Co, a unit of Philips Electronics NV said Thursday that Osram Sylvania Inc, a unit of Siemens AG has agreed to cease making claims that its yet- to-be-released low-mercury fluorescent lamps have the lowest mercury dose of any four-foot fluorescent lamp.</p>
<p>Osram, said the company, entered into the agreement to settle a suit brought by Philips to keep it from making allegedly false advertising claims comparing the mercury dose of its lamps and Philips' ALTO(TM) lamps.</p>
<p>Osram's agreement to cease making these claims, said Philips, is subject to enforcement by the United States District Court.</p>
</text>
